  (text "Y" (at 166.37 159.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 75edfbfd-7b01-471c-9081-00d2cd22be17)
  )
  (text "Input subsystem (pilink-7el.6): 4 discrete tact switches in a cross\n(UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT, d-pad style) + 4 discrete tact buttons (A/B/X/Y) --\nsee .planning/decisions/2026-11-14-dpad-instead-of-joystick.md. That ADR\nreplaced the original 5-way joystick (UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT/PRESS) with 4\nindividually-plungered switches and NO center-press switch. There is no\nPRESS/select net on this sheet -- firmware must remap select/OK onto\none of A/B/X/Y itself; that remap is firmware's job (../pico-link, not\nthis repo) and does not block this hardware design." (at 220 15 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 06d6a717-f00b-43da-b3c4-49d4780d0282)
  )
  (text "Pull resistor convention: each switch gets its own external 10k pull-up\n(R301-R308) from +3V3 to the GPIO node; the switch itself (SW301-SW308)\npulls that node to GND when pressed -- active-low, pressed = logic 0.\nThis differs from rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch's BOOTSEL/reset switches\n(SW101/SW102), which rely on the boot-ROM's own QSPI_SS handling and\nRUN's internal pull-up respectively and fit no external pull-up --\nthose are special-function pins with documented default behavior.\nOrdinary button GPIOs have no such guarantee (RP2350 GPIOs default to\nan internal pull-DOWN at power-up per rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch's own\nPSRAM_CS note), so an explicit external pull-up here keeps the input\nwell-defined before firmware configures anything, independent of\nsoftware GPIO init order." (at 220 95 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 6405952e-260e-4bf6-8c01-8d8442176dae)
  )
  (text "GPIO net assignment: GPIO20-GPIO27 (UP=20, DOWN=21, LEFT=22, RIGHT=23,\nA=24, B=25, X=26, Y=27), picked from the generic bidirectional GPIO\npool rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch exposes as global labels for every\nRP2350B GPIO not already committed to that sheet's own circuitry\n(GPIO47/PSRAM_CS is the only pin withheld from that pool). Same\ncross-sheet convention as esp32_bt.kicad_sch's ESP32_* global labels:\nsibling child sheets join same-named nets project-wide via a global\nlabel, no hierarchical sheet pins or root-sheet wiring needed. Each\nswitch also carries its firmware-facing logical name (UP/DOWN/LEFT/\nRIGHT/A/B/X/Y, the exact names given in the bead/ADR -- cross-checked\nagainst the firmware repo's input.h and confirmed matching its\nPL_INPUT_PIN_* defines (PL_INPUT_PIN_PRESS has no counterpart here,\ncorrectly, per the d-pad ADR dropping the center-press switch)) as a\nplain text caption under the switch body -- deliberately NOT a second\nschematic label on the same net: a global label and a local label\nboth landing on one net connect fine electrically, but ERC reports it\nas multiple_net_names (the global label wins in the netlist either\nway), so the logical name is documentation-only graphical text here\ninstead, with no electrical meaning and nothing for ERC to flag. No\nsibling sheet has claimed GPIO20-27 yet (display/esp32_bt/usb_c sheets\nare still empty or use their own differently-named global labels),\nconfirmed by grepping all four merged sheets before finalizing." (at 220 165 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 3c0ca8f7-c187-466d-9449-00281f05387b)
  )
  (text "Reference designators use this project's per-sheet numbering block\n300-399 (power.kicad_sch: 1-99, rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch: 100-199,\nesp32_bt.kicad_sch: 200-299) so no two sibling sheets' components can\nmerge into the same netlist part: SW301-SW308 (switches), R301-R308\n(pull-up resistors), #PWR301-#PWR316 (one +3V3 + one GND symbol per\nswitch). No PWR_FLAG on this sheet, matching rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch's\nand esp32_bt.kicad_sch's own reasoning -- this sheet doesn't generate\n+3V3/GND, power.kicad_sch does, so a standalone ERC run on this sheet\nalone is expected to report power_pin_not_driven for both rails; the\nroot sheet (which flattens the whole hierarchy and does see the\nregulator) is the real check. See hardware/README.md for both ERC\nruns and the project-wide netlist collision check.\n\nFLAG for firmware integration (out of scope here): firmware's current\nPL_INPUT_PIN_* pin NUMBERS (2/18/16/20/15/17/19/21, the old Waveshare\nboard's GPIO map) still need remapping to this schematic's GPIO20-27\nassignment -- tracked as follow-up bead pilink-otf." (at 220 235 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 9846e71a-aed5-4181-b0cc-b62ef7d1a9ec)
  )
)
